      "message": "Note to reviewers: previously, setting deltaq mode for the non-rd mode (cpu-used \u003e\u003d 8) was ignored, and functionally equivalent to turning it off `--deltaq-mode\u003d0`.\n\nWith this change, non-rd mode can now detect and set up Variance Boost `--deltaq-mode\u003d6`. Setting deltaq mode to any value other than 6 will be effectively ignored.\n\nLet me know if this is good enough. The main scenario I\u0027m focusing on is high-speed still image coding (e.g. `--cpu-used\u003d8 --tune\u003diq`).",
